Well, actually....

Frost Brand does pretty _damn_ good.  Consider...

Basically, it does double damage.  This doubling is calculated AFTER
the enchantment bonus is added in.  This means that my +8 Frost Brand,
when fighting large critters, does:

(1..12 + 8) * 2

For a maximum of 40 pts and minimum of 18.  I don't have the source
handy, but I think the blessed bonus for undead is also doubled
(although undead generally ain't large).  Once you calculate in my
strength bonus, there isn't much that doesn't go down in two or three
hits, and I _always_ hit.  Of course, I haven't met the wizard yet....
If you kill him, it only makes him mad....

Fire Brand works the same way, but has one serious problem.  It
doesn't work against fire resistant monsters, and they are almost all
fire resistant in Hell.  There are fewer cold resistant monsters,
against which Frost Brand is an ordinary sword.

